many we would expect to come back  positive  of those here's how many we would expect  to be true positives and false positives  we've got the same thing for negative  predictive value including the text here  and you can update that dynamically with  this slider  so i went from five percent prevalence  to 10 percent  and the text here has now updated so uh  you can then use that to explore  how you think uh these tests might  perform based on the data that's been  reported  uh and conditions that you believe may  affect you as an individual or  the population in your jurisdiction and  the last thing i'll point out is that  you can also download the data that's  backing up these charts  um so that you could do your own  analyses uh with the data that we  calculated  uh across the the whole range of  possible  uh infection rates here so with that  i've got a couple minutes left so i'm  going to bring us home  um you're going to see a lot of charts  like this  in the tool and basically what happened  is in  in the rush to get these diagnostic  tests out to market you know we're in an  emergency people need to move fast  what the manufacturers have gone with  have been very small  sample sizes and and often what are  called um  uh uh like spiked samples so  uh they're contrived samples so rather  than being taken from a person that  they've confirmed has coveted 19 they've  then spiked  a sample with it and so you know we see  30 positive samples 30 negative samples  all perfectly classified it doesn't mean  the test is bad or the data is bad it  just means that we don't have enough  data to really say for sure how  accurate this is um this project is  still in in active development  so you know i'd uh encourage everyone to  to that might be inclined to get  involved  check out uh copatestdb.com  covatestdb.com performance if you have  questions comments feature requests  want to help uh with data uh you can  email us covatestdb  bnx.org or you can check out our github  repository there  uh you know uh forecast on github open  up a feature request  a big team went into this that cut  across several business units at  inquitel so big thanks to them  uh and that's all my time thank you so  much thank you  tommy and he didn't disappoint with the  tweed jacket you followed through in  your word  all right i think we could all agree  covet is a very important thing we've  all been discussing  back in april when we went virtual for  the meetup very first talk was noam ross  talking about some of the math behind  epidemiology and the next month was  romney crispin talking about the the  data sources  so i think as a data community we could  all hopefully be helpful with  the this chronovirus outbreak so  that brings us up to
 

